In article <dennisb.734884691@sfu.ca> dennisb@kits.sfu.ca (Mercury Fox) writes:
>Here I am, down at level 20 (I know, not terribly great) and I come acrossed
>a alter of Alhur(sp?) and I convert it to neutral.  Succede with my first
>sacrifice.  This of course angers the priestess of Alhur, but with Vorpy, she
>is easily dispatched!  So I use my wands of crate monster, scrolls of create
>monster, and my bag of tricks to get some more sacrifices.  I sacrifice about
>20-25 more corpses.  Each time, I get a hopefull feeling or spot a 4-leaf
>clover.  But later when I am in a fight, fainting (gave my god all the corpses
>so *I* have no food), I go to pray, and my god is displeased.  WHY?????

A hopeful feeling means that you can't pray yet.  I have noticed this
while sacrificing monsters that I killed INSIDE the temple.  Monsters
refuse to attack you while you are in your own temple.  Maybe (I
haven't checked the source) it angers your god to spill blood inside
his temple, hmmm?

Lots of things increase your prayer timeout.  If you are granted an
artifact from a sacrifice, you can't pray afterwards.  If you make a
wish, you can't pray for awhile.  If you become Hand of Elbereth (or
equivalent), your timeout gets _much_ longer.

Basically, don't count on prayer.  Always make sure you can survive
one way or another, and pray only if you have no other way out.

